  "name": null,
  "problem": "Consider the finite region $R$ in the $xyz$-space, given by\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le \\frac{2x-y}{2}\\le 1,\\,0\\le \\frac{y}{2}\\le 2,\\,0\\le z\\le 3\\}.\n$$\n\nGiven the change of variables\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{2x-y}{2},\\,v=\\frac{y}{2},\\,w=\\frac{z}{3},\n$$\n\nwhich of the following could be the missing part of the expression below?\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}(\\frac{2x-y}{2}+\\frac{z}{3})\\,dV={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\bbox[3pt,border:1pt solid black]{\\phantom{AAAAAA}}\\,dw\\,dv\\,du\n$$",
  "worked_solution": "",
